  "note": "ASAP7 M8/M9 are thin (0.34 ohm/sq, the same 0.08 um pitch class as M4-M7); a production 5 nm-class stack has thick top metals (~0.02-0.04 ohm/sq) and an RDL.  At 0.1x sheet resistance the die term of the 50%-cap case falls from 16.1 to 2.2 mV per rail (32 -> 4.4 mV rail to rail).  The 'thick' rows are that sensitivity, ASSUMED ratio, not an ASAP7 result."
